+Per program, one test of the header path and one of the fallback on a header-less record (the fixtures under `tests/fixtures/workflows/`, about eighty header-less status files and the four projects' status headers, stay header-less and are the fallback's; the header path runs on copies the migration program writes in the test, so the migration is tested with each program); the reader's own tests, with the `pyyaml` cross-check over every fixture header (TASK-046) and over every header of this repository's migrated records (TASK-054's test, once they exist); the agreement check's tests per record kind (a header key changed and not the line, a line changed and not the key, a declared column renamed); the malformed cases, one per refusal, each with its line number; the `historic` exemption on a fixture shaped like the TDP's first increments and the shape noise gone, and a hand-written `historic: true` on an unmerged increment refused (`plan-check.py` exempts a historic increment only where its own merged set, read from its `--base`, holds the ID; under `--no-git`, or where the log cannot be read, it accepts the mark with a note, never a failure); a currency test, at the last program increment, that every fallback reader in `bridge_env` has a key in `HEADER_SCHEMAS` and every key a stated type, and that no program keeps a retired reading of the enumerated list, matched as a use with docstrings and comments stripped (the plan's first acceptance clause as a test; the row R-057 flips built there, at TASK-050, the later of its increments); `tests/test_header_schemas.py` against D-005; the `dump_cli` test against D-002's edges as revised; the token measure, over this repository's status file and one brief, `handoff/TASK-046.md`: measured once in the supervisor's checkout before the push, each file's bytes at the trim's commit and at the migration's commit and its header's bytes, read by `git show <sha>:<path>`, the numbers quoted in the accept commit and written as constants